# ⚛️ React Interview Questions & Answers

---

# 1️⃣ How do you send data from a parent component to a child component?

Data is passed from parent to child using **props**.

### Parent Component

```jsx
function Parent() {
  const name = "Hari";

  return <Child name={name} />;
}
```

### Child Component

```jsx
function Child({ name }) {
  return <h1>{name}</h1>;
}
```

### Use Cases

- Passing user data
- Configuration settings
- API response data

---

# 2️⃣ How do you call a parent component method from a child component?

Pass the parent method as a prop.

### Parent

```jsx
function Parent() {
  const showMessage = () => {
    alert("Hello from Parent");
  };

  return <Child onClick={showMessage} />;
}
```

### Child

```jsx
function Child({ onClick }) {
  return (
    <button onClick={onClick}>
      Click
    </button>
  );
}
```

---

# 3️⃣ How do you access a DOM element in React?

Using **useRef**.

```jsx
import { useRef } from "react";

function App() {
  const inputRef = useRef();

  const focusInput = () => {
    inputRef.current.focus();
  };

  return (
    <>
      <input ref={inputRef} />
      <button onClick={focusInput}>
        Focus
      </button>
    </>
  );
}
```

### Use Cases

- Focus inputs
- Video controls
- Scroll handling

---

# 4️⃣ How to conditionally render elements or text?

### Using Ternary Operator

```jsx
function App() {
  const isLoggedIn = true;

  return (
    <>
      {isLoggedIn
        ? <h1>Welcome</h1>
        : <h1>Please Login</h1>}
    </>
  );
}
```

---

### Using &&

```jsx
{
  isLoggedIn &&
  <h1>Dashboard</h1>
}
```

---

# 5️⃣ How to change styles based on a condition?

```jsx
function App() {
  const isActive = true;

  return (
    <button
      style={{
        backgroundColor: isActive
          ? "green"
          : "gray"
      }}
    >
      Submit
    </button>
  );
}
```

### Using CSS Classes

```jsx
<button
  className={
    isActive
      ? "active"
      : "inactive"
  }
>
  Submit
</button>
```

---

# 6️⃣ How to show and hide data conditionally?

```jsx
function App() {
  const [show, setShow] =
    useState(false);

  return (
    <>
      <button
        onClick={() =>
          setShow(!show)
        }
      >
        Toggle
      </button>

      {show && (
        <p>Hidden Content</p>
      )}
    </>
  );
}
```

---

# 7️⃣ How to implement debouncing in React?

```jsx
import { useEffect, useState } from "react";

function Search() {
  const [query, setQuery] =
    useState("");

  const [debounced,
    setDebounced] =
    useState("");

  useEffect(() => {

    const timer =
      setTimeout(() => {
        setDebounced(query);
      }, 500);

    return () =>
      clearTimeout(timer);

  }, [query]);

  return (
    <input
      value={query}
      onChange={(e) =>
        setQuery(e.target.value)
      }
    />
  );
}
```

### Use Cases

- Search bars
- API calls
- Auto-save

---

# 8️⃣ How to fetch data from an API and display it?

```jsx
import {
  useEffect,
  useState
} from "react";

function Users() {

  const [users, setUsers] =
    useState([]);

  useEffect(() => {

    fetch(
      "https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/users"
    )
      .then(res => res.json())
      .then(data =>
        setUsers(data)
      );

  }, []);

  return (
    <>
      {users.map(user => (
        <p key={user.id}>
          {user.name}
        </p>
      ))}
    </>
  );
}
```

---

# 9️⃣ How to re-render a component on value change?

React automatically re-renders when:

- State changes
- Props change
- Context changes

```jsx
const [count, setCount] =
  useState(0);

setCount(count + 1);
```

---

# 🔟 How to call a method immediately after state updates?

### Using useEffect

```jsx
const [count, setCount] =
  useState(0);

useEffect(() => {
  console.log(
    "Count Updated",
    count
  );
}, [count]);
```

### Equivalent to

```javascript
componentDidUpdate()
```

---

# 1️⃣1️⃣ How to force a component to rerender without useState?

Using useReducer.

```jsx
const [, forceUpdate] =
  useReducer(x => x + 1, 0);

<button
  onClick={forceUpdate}
>
  Refresh
</button>
```

---

# 1️⃣2️⃣ Optimization Using useMemo

Used for expensive calculations.

```jsx
const total = useMemo(() => {

  console.log("Calculating");

  return products.reduce(
    (sum, item) =>
      sum + item.price,
    0
  );

}, [products]);
```

### Benefits

- Avoids recalculation
- Improves performance

---

# 1️⃣3️⃣ Optimization Using useCallback

Prevents unnecessary function recreation.

```jsx
const handleClick =
  useCallback(() => {

    console.log("Clicked");

  }, []);
```

### Useful With

```jsx
React.memo()
```

---

# 1️⃣4️⃣ Which lifecycle methods are replaced by useEffect?

| Class Lifecycle | useEffect Equivalent |
|-----------------|----------------------|
| componentDidMount | useEffect(() => {}, []) |
| componentDidUpdate | useEffect(() => {}, [dependency]) |
| componentWillUnmount | Cleanup Function |

### Example

```jsx
useEffect(() => {

  return () => {
    console.log(
      "Component Removed"
    );
  };

}, []);
```

---

# 1️⃣5️⃣ How to share data using Context API?

### Create Context

```jsx
import {
  createContext
} from "react";

export const UserContext =
  createContext();
```

---

### Provider

```jsx
<UserContext.Provider
  value={user}
>
  <App />
</UserContext.Provider>
```

---

### Consume

```jsx
const user =
  useContext(UserContext);
```

---

# 1️⃣6️⃣ How do you create a custom hook?

```jsx
import {
  useState
} from "react";

function useCounter() {

  const [count,
    setCount] =
    useState(0);

  const increment =
    () =>
      setCount(
        count + 1
      );

  return {
    count,
    increment
  };
}
```

### Usage

```jsx
const {
  count,
  increment
} = useCounter();
```

---

# 1️⃣7️⃣ How do you create a lazy-loaded component?

```jsx
import {
  lazy,
  Suspense
} from "react";

const Dashboard =
  lazy(() =>
    import("./Dashboard")
  );

function App() {
  return (
    <Suspense
      fallback={<h1>Loading...</h1>}
    >
      <Dashboard />
    </Suspense>
  );
}
```

### Benefits

- Smaller bundle size
- Faster initial load

---

# 1️⃣8️⃣ How do you build a pagination component?

```jsx
function Pagination({
  totalPages,
  currentPage,
  setCurrentPage
}) {

  return (
    <>
      {[...Array(totalPages)]
        .map((_, index) => (

          <button
            key={index}
            onClick={() =>
              setCurrentPage(
                index + 1
              )
            }
          >
            {index + 1}
          </button>

      ))}
    </>
  );
}
```

