# 2️⃣0️⃣ Controlled vs Uncontrolled Components

## Controlled Component

React controls input state.

```jsx
function App() {

  const [name,
    setName] =
    useState("");

  return (
    <input
      value={name}
      onChange={(e) =>
        setName(
          e.target.value
        )
      }
    />
  );
}
```

### Benefits

- Validation
- Predictable state

---

## Uncontrolled Component

DOM controls input value.

```jsx
function App() {

  const inputRef =
    useRef();

  const submit = () => {
    console.log(
      inputRef.current.value
    );
  };

  return (
    <>
      <input ref={inputRef} />

      <button
        onClick={submit}
      >
        Submit
      </button>
    </>
  );
}
```

### Comparison

| Controlled | Uncontrolled |
|------------|-------------|
| React manages state | DOM manages state |
| More control | Simpler |
| Easier validation | Less code |

---
